From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-broker: the broker names the call its client lock's holder waits in

In a 2026-10-15 run (record removed from the tree; in git history) the broker's client lock was found held at every flight-recorder sample from t=40 to t=278
(broker=busy:239, fences 6881/6881: the GPU had finished everything it was given) and the console froze; an emulator
session before salvage-20261015-092043 held it from t=75 to its last row at t=328.7 (busy:252, fences 21073/21073); in
two more 2026-10-15 runs it was held 16 and 15 s and cleared. Nothing recorded which
call the holder was in. Each call that can wait while that lock is held now sets an atomic phase, its start and the
holder's thread around itself: drain, reap-free, stage-alloc, copy (the memcpy of the client's command words, from
memory shared with the helper), submit, suspend, alloc, map, grant, munmap and give-back. ps5_gpu_broker_health
reads them with atomics alone, never the client or display lock (0012's rule), for the title's flight recorder.
PROTON_TEST_BROKER_HOLD_S=n holds the client lock n s once, 10 s after the first submission, in phase test-hold, so
the title's wedge rule (PS5_Proton src/pw_hang_breaker.h) can be shown on the console without a real GPU hang.

The client gives the broker up for good in one place, broker_lost: no answer in 15 s, the connection closed or failed,
a reply that is not the answer, or a free the broker did not take back. Only the first transition (one atomic
exchange) writes a line saying why and stamps the helper's GPU reason through PS5_Proton ntdll's pw_ps5_child_doomed,
after which the helper's loader ends the process in 5 s; the 2026-10-15 run's helper never ended after its 15 s
give-up and the console froze. The stamp is looked up once, in bind, outside the rpc lock, with the symbol lookup
PS5_Proton's Wine module loader hands this module as it opens it (pw_module_lookup): the client's own dlsym is
libkernel's, not Wine's, and the firmware's lookup finds no application module's export (sceKernelDlsym on 12.02,
PS5_Proton tools/gen_prx_descriptor.py). Without one (a title's process, a host build) nothing is
stamped. A refusal the broker answers is not a loss. Wine patch 1135 stamped the GPU reason at any
VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST in win32u instead, and in gate-hang-a-2026-10-15-01 (72 of 75 passed) gpu-window32 and
gpu-window64 each logged "payload doom seen reason=gpu" when the broker answered the first three (32-bit) and two
(64-bit) window presents with status 70 (ESTALE); both programs presented on (40 and 39 frames by the broker's pacing
lines) and their helpers ended by themselves about 2 s later. A game that rebuilds its window or swapchain, or
recreates its device after DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED, would have been ended 5 s after such a result. Not yet run on the
console.
---
diff --git a/tooling/gpu-broker/client.c b/tooling/gpu-broker/client.c
index 5bc7546..d0eb5ce 100644
--- a/tooling/gpu-broker/client.c
+++ b/tooling/gpu-broker/client.c
@@ -72,6 +72,27 @@ int ps5_gpu_client_done(int result,uint64_t images,uint64_t hash);
 int ps5_gpu_client_image(unsigned cycle,unsigned pixels,uint64_t hash);
 int ps5_gpu_client_coherence(unsigned slot,unsigned words,uint64_t hash);
 int ps5_gpu_client_timing(unsigned slot,unsigned count,uint64_t ns);
+void pw_module_lookup(void *(*lookup)(void *,const char *));
+/* PS5_Proton's helper loader ends the process 5 s after its GPU reason is stamped (ntdll's pw_ps5_child_doomed(1),
+ * PW_CHILD_DOOM_GPU). The module loader that opens this module in a helper hands it its own symbol lookup: this
+ * module's dlsym is libkernel's, and the firmware's lookup finds no application module's export (sceKernelDlsym on
+ * 12.02). bind resolves the stamp with it, outside the rpc lock. None (a title's process, a host build): no stamp. */
+static void *(*module_lookup)(void *,const char *);
+static void (*doomed)(unsigned);
+void pw_module_lookup(void *(*lookup)(void *,const char *)) { module_lookup=lookup; }
+/* The client gives the broker up for good: from here every call fails at once and the program sees its device lost.
+ * Only a loss does this: no answer in 15 s (the broker stuck under its lock, as when a 2026-10-15 run froze the
+ * console), the connection gone, a reply that is not the answer, or a free the broker did not take back. A call the
+ * broker answered with a refusal is none: in gate-hang-a-2026-10-15-01 it answered a helper's first two window presents
+ * with status 70 (ESTALE), the program presented on (39 frames in 2.1 s) and ended by itself, and a game that rebuilds
+ * its window, swapchain or device goes on the same way. The first transition alone says why and stamps
+ * the GPU reason (one compare-exchange, safe under the rpc lock). */
+static void broker_lost(const char *why,unsigned operation,unsigned sequence)
+{
+    if(__atomic_exchange_n(&broken,1,__ATOMIC_RELAXED))return;
+    fprintf(stderr,"gpu-client: the broker is given up on: %s (operation %u sequence %u)\n",why,operation,sequence);
+    if(doomed)doomed(1 /* PW_CHILD_DOOM_GPU */);
+}
 /* For SUBMIT round trips: the time spent taking the lock, sending, and waiting for the reply to be readable. */
 static uint64_t rpc_lock_ns,rpc_send_ns,rpc_wait_ns;
 void ps5_gpu_client_rpc_split(uint64_t split[3])
@@ -94,16 +115,18 @@ static int rpc(PwGpuMessage *message,int *descriptor)
     /* The owner answers in tens of microseconds, so the reply is looked for by peeking: continuously for 2 ms, then
      * after short polls, which bound the wait for one that takes longer. Adopted while poll was suspected of waking
      * late (graphics-child-gpu-async-07 to -13); those stalls were the owner's disk writes under its lock (async-18). */
-    int readable=0;
+    int readable=0;const char *lost=sent ? "a reply that is not the answer" : "the send failed";
     if(sent) {
         const uint64_t start=radv_ps5_now_ns(),spin_until=start+2000000,give_up=start+15000000000ull;
         char peek=0;
         for(;;) {
             const ssize_t found=recv(broker,&peek,1,MSG_PEEK|MSG_DONTWAIT);
             if(found==1) { readable=1;break; }
-            if(found==0 || (found<0 && errno!=EAGAIN && errno!=EWOULDBLOCK && errno!=EINTR))break;
+            if(found==0 || (found<0 && errno!=EAGAIN && errno!=EWOULDBLOCK && errno!=EINTR)) {
+                lost=found ? "the connection failed" : "the connection closed";break;
+            }
             const uint64_t now=radv_ps5_now_ns();
-            if(now>=give_up)break;
+            if(now>=give_up) { lost="no answer in 15 s";break; }
             /* Yield, not pause: the owner's thread serving this client may share its CPU. */
             if(now<spin_until)sched_yield();
             else poll(&p,1,1);
@@ -121,13 +144,15 @@ static int rpc(PwGpuMessage *message,int *descriptor)
          (operation==PW_GPU_ALLOC && descriptor && !message->status && !count && message->argument[2]));
     if(okay && descriptor) *descriptor=count ? fds[0] : -1;
     else for(unsigned i=0;i<count;++i)close(fds[i]);
-    if(!okay)__atomic_store_n(&broken,1,__ATOMIC_RELAXED);
+    if(!okay)broker_lost(lost,operation,expected);
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
     return okay ? message->status : EIO;
 }
 int ps5_gpu_client_bind(int fd, bool reserved)
 {
     if(broker>=0 || fd<0)return -1;
+    /* NULL: every module loaded, as Wine's dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT). */
+    if(module_lookup)doomed=(void (*)(unsigned))module_lookup(NULL,"pw_ps5_child_doomed");
     broker=fd;
     ranges_reserved=reserved;
     /* argument[2]: whether this process reserved the host ranges, for the owner's log. */
@@ -331,7 +356,7 @@ void radv_ps5_memory_free(struct radv_ps5_memory *memory)
         if(source_find((uintptr_t)memory->cpu,true,&source) && source.fd>=0)close(source.fd);
     }
     /* Broker submissions complete before acknowledgment; no GPU references remain. */
-    if(rpc(&message,NULL)) { __atomic_store_n(&broken,1,__ATOMIC_RELAXED);return; }
+    if(rpc(&message,NULL)) { broker_lost("a free it did not take back",PW_GPU_FREE,message.sequence);return; }
     if(memory->physical==PS5_GPU_LOCAL_MEMORY)__atomic_sub_fetch(&local_allocated,memory->bytes,__ATOMIC_RELAXED);
     else __atomic_sub_fetch(&allocated,memory->bytes,__ATOMIC_RELAXED);
     memset(memory,0,sizeof(*memory));
diff --git a/tooling/gpu-broker/client.h b/tooling/gpu-broker/client.h
index e317c83..aafa935 100644
--- a/tooling/gpu-broker/client.h
+++ b/tooling/gpu-broker/client.h
@@ -15,6 +15,11 @@ int ps5_gpu_client_bind(int fd,bool reserved);
  * WoW64 maps all of its memory below 4 GiB): call before Vulkan allocates. The client then keeps each host-visible
  * allocation's direct-memory offset, which a placed mapping needs; without it none is kept and nothing is placed. */
 void ps5_gpu_client_keep_sources(void);
+/* For PS5_Proton's Wine module loader (its wine/ps5/pw_wine_dl.h), which calls it with its own symbol lookup as it
+ * opens this module: bind then looks up ntdll's pw_ps5_child_doomed, which the client calls once, when it gives the
+ * broker up for good (no answer in 15 s, the connection gone, a malformed reply, a free not taken back), so the
+ * helper's loader ends the process 5 s later. Never called (a title's process, a host build): nothing is stamped. */
+void pw_module_lookup(void *(*lookup)(void *,const char *));
 int ps5_gpu_client_done(int result,uint64_t images,uint64_t hash);
 int ps5_gpu_client_image(unsigned cycle,unsigned pixels,uint64_t hash);
 int ps5_gpu_client_coherence(unsigned slot,unsigned words,uint64_t hash);
diff --git a/tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp b/tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp
index 977ddc3..2446cc9 100644
--- a/tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp
+++ b/tooling/gpu-broker/server.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "display.h"
 
 #include <pthread.h>
+#include <pthread_np.h>
 
 extern "C" {
 #include "radv_ps5_platform.h"
@@ -238,6 +239,33 @@ bool give_up(FILE *out,const char *reason)
 // PROTON_GPU_TEST_FAIL_SUBMIT=n (Wine broker): the submission after n succeeds is refused before it reaches the GPU,
 // as a failed one would be, to show the title surviving a broker failure. 0: off.
 unsigned test_fail_submit=0,test_submissions=0;
+// The call the client lock's holder waits in, for an application's watchdog (ps5_gpu_broker_health), which reads these
+// with atomics and never the lock. A 2026-10-15 run held b.lock from flight-recorder t=40 to t=278 with every
+// fence completed, and nothing said in which call. Set around each call that can wait while b.lock is held and the
+// outer one restored after, always within one stretch of holding it (never across the unlock a present makes), so the
+// outermost restores none.
+std::atomic<const char *> held_phase{nullptr};
+std::atomic<uint64_t> held_since_ns{0};
+std::atomic<int> held_tid{0};
+struct Phase {
+    const char *outer;uint64_t outer_since;int outer_tid;
+    explicit Phase(const char *name):outer(held_phase.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)),
+        outer_since(held_since_ns.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)),outer_tid(held_tid.load(std::memory_order_relaxed))
+    {
+        held_tid.store(pthread_getthreadid_np(),std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        held_since_ns.store(radv_ps5_now_ns(),std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        held_phase.store(name,std::memory_order_release);
+    }
+    ~Phase()
+    {
+        held_tid.store(outer_tid,std::memory_order_relaxed);held_since_ns.store(outer_since,std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        held_phase.store(outer,std::memory_order_release);
+    }
+};
+// PROTON_TEST_BROKER_HOLD_S=n (Wine broker): once, the first submission 10 s after the first one keeps the client lock
+// n s longer, in phase test-hold, as a broker stuck in a kernel call would: the title's wedge rule ends the game
+// (src/pw_hang_breaker.h). Under b.lock. 0: off.
+unsigned test_hold_s=0;uint64_t test_hold_first_ns=0;bool test_held=false;
 bool owned(const Client &c,uint64_t address,uint64_t bytes)
 {
     for(const auto &b:c.buffers)if(b.token && pw_gpu_contains(b.address,b.bytes,address,bytes))return true;
@@ -252,6 +280,7 @@ int (*dmem_release)(int64_t offset,size_t bytes)=nullptr;
 unsigned long long dmem_made=0,dmem_freed=0,dmem_refused=0,dmem_free_failed=0,dmem_bytes_made=0;
 void dmem_give_back(int64_t offset,uint64_t bytes)
 {
+    Phase phase("give-back");
     if(dmem_release && !dmem_release(offset,(size_t)bytes))++dmem_freed;
     else ++dmem_free_failed;
 }
@@ -260,6 +289,7 @@ void dmem_give_back(int64_t offset,uint64_t bytes)
 int shared_object(uint64_t bytes);
 void *map_host(const Client &c,void *at,uint64_t bytes,int &fd,int64_t &dmem)
 {
+    Phase phase("map");
     fd=-1;dmem=-1;
     // Direct memory first; a range the helper refuses (the pool is full, a grant failed) or this process cannot map is made as a
     // shared-memory object instead, which the client maps by descriptor as before.
@@ -279,6 +309,7 @@ void *map_host(const Client &c,void *at,uint64_t bytes,int &fd,int64_t &dmem)
 }
 void release(Buffer &b)
 {
+    Phase phase("munmap");
     if(b.local)radv_ps5_memory_free(&b.memory);
     else if(b.ranged) {
         // Back to a reservation laid over the mapping (it replaces it), and the range back to the free list.
@@ -325,8 +356,11 @@ int allocate_local(Client &c,PwGpuMessage &m,Buffer &b,uint64_t bytes,uint64_t a
     if(radv_ps5_memory_available_bytes()<kLocalFloor+bytes)return ENOMEM;
     c.allocation_stage="local_direct";
     radv_ps5_memory memory{};
-    if(!radv_ps5_memory_alloc(bytes,alignment,m.argument[1]!=0,&memory))return ENOMEM;
-    if(m.argument[2]&PW_GPU_ALLOC_ZERO) { memset(memory.cpu,0,memory.bytes);radv_ps5_cpu_flush(memory.cpu,memory.bytes); }
+    {
+        Phase phase("alloc");
+        if(!radv_ps5_memory_alloc(bytes,alignment,m.argument[1]!=0,&memory))return ENOMEM;
+        if(m.argument[2]&PW_GPU_ALLOC_ZERO) { memset(memory.cpu,0,memory.bytes);radv_ps5_cpu_flush(memory.cpu,memory.bytes); }
+    }
     b=Buffer{(uint64_t)memory.cpu,memory.bytes,++c.next_token,-1,true,false,memory};
     c.local+=memory.bytes;if(c.local>c.local_peak)c.local_peak=c.local;
     m.address=b.address;m.bytes=b.bytes;m.argument[0]=b.token;
@@ -355,8 +389,9 @@ int allocate(Client &c,PwGpuMessage &m,uint64_t &next_window,uint64_t &next_high
         int shared=-1;int64_t dmem=-1;
         void *mapped=map_host(c,(void *)address,bytes,shared,dmem);
         bool granted=mapped==(void *)address;
-        if(granted) { c.allocation_stage="gpu_permissions";granted=radv_ps5_memory_grant_gpu(mapped,bytes); }
+        if(granted) { c.allocation_stage="gpu_permissions";Phase phase("grant");granted=radv_ps5_memory_grant_gpu(mapped,bytes); }
         if(!granted) {
+            Phase phase("munmap");
             void *at=(void *)address;
             if(!sceKernelReserveVirtualRange(&at,bytes,PW_GPU_RESERVE_FIXED,16384) && at==(void *)address)range.give(address,bytes);
             if(shared>=0)close(shared);
@@ -387,8 +422,9 @@ int allocate(Client &c,PwGpuMessage &m,uint64_t &next_window,uint64_t &next_high
     int shared=-1;int64_t dmem=-1;
     void *mapped=map_host(c,reserved,bytes,shared,dmem);
     bool granted=false;
-    if(mapped==reserved) { c.allocation_stage="gpu_permissions";granted=radv_ps5_memory_grant_gpu(mapped,bytes); }
+    if(mapped==reserved) { c.allocation_stage="gpu_permissions";Phase phase("grant");granted=radv_ps5_memory_grant_gpu(mapped,bytes); }
     if(!granted) {
+        Phase phase("munmap");
         sceKernelMunmap(reserved,bytes);if(shared>=0)close(shared);if(dmem>=0)dmem_give_back(dmem,bytes);return ENOMEM;
     }
     *b=Buffer{address,bytes,++c.next_token,shared};b->dmem=dmem;b->pid=c.pid;c.allocated+=bytes;cursor=address+bytes;
@@ -428,6 +464,7 @@ int broker_submit(void *words,uint32_t count)
 void kick()
 {
     if(!fences.kick)return;
+    Phase phase("suspend");
     const uint64_t start=radv_ps5_now_ns();
     sceAgcSuspendPoint();
     fences.kick_ns+=radv_ps5_now_ns()-start;++fences.kicks;fences.kick=false;
@@ -444,6 +481,7 @@ void reap()
     if(!fences.page.cpu)return;
     const uint32_t now=completed();
     while(fences.count && done(fences.ring[fences.head].seq,now)) {
+        Phase phase("reap-free");
         radv_ps5_memory_free(&fences.ring[fences.head].staging);
         fences.ring[fences.head]=Inflight{};fences.head=(fences.head+1)%Fences::kRing;--fences.count;
     }
@@ -457,6 +495,7 @@ bool drain(uint64_t timeout_ns)
 {
     reap();
     if(!fences.count && !fences.deferred_count)return true;
+    Phase phase("drain");
     ++fences.drains;
     const uint64_t end=radv_ps5_now_ns()+timeout_ns;
     while((fences.count || fences.deferred_count) && radv_ps5_now_ns()<end) { sceKernelUsleep(50);reap(); }
@@ -513,12 +552,20 @@ int submit(Client &c,const PwGpuMessage &m,FILE *out,unsigned client)
     }
     const uint64_t t1=radv_ps5_now_ns();c.time_wait+=t1-t0;
     radv_ps5_memory staging{};
-    if(!radv_ps5_memory_alloc(m.bytes+32,16384,false,&staging))return ENOMEM;
-    memcpy(staging.cpu,(void *)m.address,m.bytes);
+    {
+        Phase phase("stage-alloc");
+        if(!radv_ps5_memory_alloc(m.bytes+32,16384,false,&staging))return ENOMEM;
+    }
+    {
+        // The client's command words, in memory it shares with this process.
+        Phase phase("copy");
+        memcpy(staging.cpu,(void *)m.address,m.bytes);
+    }
     uint32_t seq=__atomic_add_fetch(&fences.issued,1,__ATOMIC_RELAXED);if(!seq)seq=__atomic_add_fetch(&fences.issued,1,__ATOMIC_RELAXED);
     ps5_gpu_completion_packet((uint32_t *)((uint8_t *)staging.cpu+m.bytes),(uint64_t)fences.page.cpu,seq);
     const uint64_t t2=radv_ps5_now_ns();c.time_stage+=t2-t1;
     int status=0;
+    Phase phase("submit");
     if(tess_changes && !(status=radv_ps5_set_tess_factor_ring(c.tess,c.tess_bytes))) { fences.tess=c.tess;fences.tess_bytes=c.tess_bytes; }
     if(!status && offchip_changes && !(status=radv_ps5_set_hs_offchip_param(c.granularity,c.buffering))) {
         fences.offchip=true;fences.granularity=c.granularity;fences.buffering=c.buffering;
@@ -730,7 +777,19 @@ void *client_main(void *argument)
                     free_buffer(c,a,b.log);m.status=0;break;
                 }
                 break;
-            case PW_GPU_SUBMIT: m.status=submit(c,m,b.log,c.cookie);break;
+            case PW_GPU_SUBMIT:
+                m.status=submit(c,m,b.log,c.cookie);
+                if(test_hold_s && !test_held) {
+                    const uint64_t now=radv_ps5_now_ns();
+                    if(!test_hold_first_ns)test_hold_first_ns=now;
+                    else if(now-test_hold_first_ns>=10000000000ull) {
+                        test_held=true;
+                        fprintf(b.log,"gpu-broker test_hold=%u s pid=%d\n",test_hold_s,c.pid);
+                        Phase hold("test-hold");
+                        for(unsigned second=0;second<test_hold_s;++second)sceKernelUsleep(1000000);
+                    }
+                }
+                break;
             case PW_GPU_TESS:
                 if(m.bytes<=UINT32_MAX && owned(c,m.address,m.bytes)) { c.tess=m.address;c.tess_bytes=(uint32_t)m.bytes;m.status=0; }break;
             case PW_GPU_OFFCHIP:
@@ -990,6 +1049,11 @@ void ps5_gpu_broker_health(Ps5GpuBrokerHealth *health)
     health->display_busy=pthread_mutex_trylock(&b.display_lock)!=0;
     if(!health->display_busy)pthread_mutex_unlock(&b.display_lock);
     health->fences_issued=__atomic_load_n(&fences.issued,__ATOMIC_RELAXED);
+    if((health->phase=held_phase.load(std::memory_order_acquire))) {
+        const uint64_t since=held_since_ns.load(std::memory_order_relaxed),now=radv_ps5_now_ns();
+        health->phase_ms=now>since ? (now-since)/1000000 : 0;
+        health->holder_tid=held_tid.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    }
     pthread_mutex_lock(&fence_page_lock);
     if(fences.page.cpu)health->fences_completed=completed();
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&fence_page_lock);
@@ -1059,8 +1123,9 @@ bool ps5_gpu_broker_start(const char *directory,bool capture,bool local,bool (*i
     b.local_memory=local;
     retain_on_failure=false;wedged=false;test_submissions=0;
     {
-        const char *fail=getenv("PROTON_GPU_TEST_FAIL_SUBMIT");
+        const char *fail=getenv("PROTON_GPU_TEST_FAIL_SUBMIT"),*hold=getenv("PROTON_TEST_BROKER_HOLD_S");
         test_fail_submit=fail ? (unsigned)strtoul(fail,nullptr,10) : 0;
+        test_hold_s=hold ? (unsigned)strtoul(hold,nullptr,10) : 0;test_hold_first_ns=0;test_held=false;
     }
     b.log_file=fopen(output_path("/app0/gpu-broker-results.txt").c_str(),"w");
     if(!b.log_file) { fprintf(stderr,"gpu-wine startup stage=open errno=%d\n",errno);return false; }
@@ -1074,7 +1139,7 @@ bool ps5_gpu_broker_start(const char *directory,bool capture,bool local,bool (*i
         b.capture_every=every ? (unsigned)strtoul(every,nullptr,10) : 0;
     }
     host_ranges_reserve(b.log);
-    fprintf(b.log,"gpu-wine broker test_fail_submit=%u capture_every=%u\n",test_fail_submit,b.capture_every);
+    fprintf(b.log,"gpu-wine broker test_fail_submit=%u capture_every=%u test_hold_s=%u\n",test_fail_submit,b.capture_every,test_hold_s);
     fprintf(b.log,"gpu-wine broker local_memory=%d local_offer=%llu local_floor=%llu host_limit=%llu\n",local,
         (unsigned long long)(local ? local_offer() : 0),(unsigned long long)kLocalFloor,(unsigned long long)host_limit);
     b.holder=b.holder_pid=0;b.switches=b.hidden=0;b.compositor_stop=false;
diff --git a/tooling/gpu-broker/server.h b/tooling/gpu-broker/server.h
index da27895..5a00fc4 100644
--- a/tooling/gpu-broker/server.h
+++ b/tooling/gpu-broker/server.h
@@ -29,8 +29,11 @@ unsigned long long ps5_gpu_broker_flips(void);
 bool ps5_gpu_broker_capture_next(const char *path);
 /* The broker as of now, for an application's watchdog, without waiting on anything the broker holds: whether its
  * client lock and its display lock are held this instant (a trylock, released at once), the GPU submissions it made
- * and the last one the GPU completed (its fence page's value; 0 before the first submission). Any thread. */
-struct Ps5GpuBrokerHealth { unsigned lock_busy,display_busy,fences_issued,fences_completed; };
+ * and the last one the GPU completed (its fence page's value; 0 before the first submission). phase is the call the
+ * client lock's holder waits in (drain, reap-free, stage-alloc, copy, submit, suspend, alloc, map, grant, munmap,
+ * give-back, test-hold; null when in none of them), since phase_ms ago, on thread holder_tid: read with atomics alone.
+ * Any thread. */
+struct Ps5GpuBrokerHealth { unsigned lock_busy,display_busy,fences_issued,fences_completed;const char *phase;unsigned long long phase_ms;int holder_tid; };
